<div class="section" id="update-freshness">
    <h2>4. Retailer Reporting Freshness Analysis</h2>

    <p>The <strong>update lag</strong> — the time difference between when a retailer last updated their price (<code>source_updated_at</code>) and when it was captured by the data collection system (<code>recorded_at</code>) — is a measure of reporting freshness. Shorter lags indicate more timely reporting and better data quality for consumers and policymakers relying on the open data feed.</p>

